  {:id :nlab-condition-2,
   :statement
   "equipped with a collection of triangles called distinguished triangles (dts).",
   :refs [:additive-category]}
  {:id :nlab-condition-3,
   :statement
   "such that the following axioms hold TR0: every triangle isomorphic to a distinguished triangle is itself a distinguished triangle; TR1: the triangle X X 0 T X is a distinguished triangle; TR2: for all f : X Y, there exists a distinguished triangle X Y Z T X \\,; TR3: a triangle X Y Z T X is a distinguished triangle precisely if Y Z T X T Y is a distinguished triangle; TR4: given two distinguished triangles X Y Z T X and X' Y' Z' T X' and given morphisms and in & Y \\\\ ^ && ^ \\\\ X' && Y' there exists a morphism : Z Z' extending this to a morphism of distinguished triangles in that the diagram & Y && Z && T X \\\\ ^ && ^ && ^ && ^ \\\\ X' && Y' && Z' && T X' commutes; TR5 (octahedral axiom): given three distinguished triangles of the form & X Y Y/X T X \\\\ & Y Z Z/Y T Y \\\\ & X Z Z/X T X there exists a distinguished triangle Y/X Z/X Z/Y T (Y/X) such that the following big diagram commutes && Z &&&& Z/Y &&&& T (Y/X) \\\\ & f && && ^l && && ^ && \\\\ && Y &&&& Z/X &&&& T Y \\\\ &&& ^h && && ^ && _T(f) \\\\ &&&& Y/X &&&& T X If TR5 is not required, one speaks of a pretriangulated category.",
   :refs [:additive-category]}],
